-<section><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem 0"><p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:680px;line-height:1.75">Myrtle Beach is the core of the Grand Strand and carries its deepest tourist demand. Inventory ranges widely, from oceanfront and resort condominiums to single-family neighborhoods further inland, which gives investors the broadest set of price points and strategies in the region.</p></div></section>
-<section style="background:var(--ivory)"><div style="max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem"><p style="font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem">Common Questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1.5rem">Frequently asked questions</h2><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Can you short-term rental (Airbnb) a house in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Usually not. The City of Myrtle Beach prohibits rentals under 90 days in all R (residential) zoning districts except RMV, and treats STRs as a commercial use. You generally need a property in an STR-eligible tourist or RMV zone and a business license. Lodging taxes and fees on the rent total 13 percent inside the city.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What counts as a short-term rental in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">The city defines a short-term rental as any stay under 90 days. South Carolina uses the same 90-day line for its lodging tax.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's or seller's market?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It leans toward buyers in early-to-mid 2026, especially in the condo segment, where inventory sits around seven to eight months of supply and gives buyers negotiating room.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What are property taxes on a second home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Higher than on a primary residence. A primary home is taxed on 4 percent of its value and does not pay the school operating tax. A second home is taxed on 6 percent and pays the school operating tax. In the city of Myrtle Beach that makes a second home's bill about 3.8 times a primary home's on the same house.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Which schools serve Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">Public schools fall within the Myrtle Beach attendance area of Horry County Schools. Assignment is by address, and Chapter3 will confirm the exact schools on the district boundary map.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">Is Myrtle Beach good for short-term rentals?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">It has the region&#x27;s deepest tourist demand, especially near the oceanfront, though performance and short-term-rental rules vary by area and building.</p></div><div style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule);padding:1.4rem 0"><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:.5rem">What property types are common in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:680px">A broad mix, from oceanfront and resort condominiums to single-family neighborhoods inland.</p></div></div></section>
