+</style><style>main#main .hx-strip:empty{display:none}main#main .hx-strip:not(:empty)+.hx-fallback{display:none}</style><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Only in the zones where the city allows it. Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, any rental shorter than 90 days counts as a short-term rental, the kind people book on Airbnb.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every zoning district whose name starts with R, for residential, bans them, except RMV, the one for visitor apartments. A house outside the allowed zones cannot be switched over or approved for nightly rentals. Breaking the rule is a misdemeanor, with a fine of up to $500, up to 30 days in jail, or both, for each violation.</p><figure class="c3-mb-fig" id="rental-map"><div class="c3-mb-frame"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/nightly-rental-zones-map.svg" width="760" height="717" alt="Map of the City of Myrtle Beach, a long strip along the ocean. Orange areas allow nightly rentals: most of the oceanfront, the Broadway at the Beach area and stretches of the main roads inland. Green areas are zoned for homes only and do not. Numbers mark 1 Grande Dunes at the north end, 2 The Market Common at the south end, 3 the older neighborhoods of houses north of downtown, and 4 the oceanfront condos. The airport is inside the city." loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><figcaption><ul class="c3-mb-legend" aria-label="Map colors"><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Nightly rentals allowed</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#5f8a6e"></span>Zoned for homes: no rentals under 90 days</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#d9cfa6"></span>Planned communities, not allowed</li><li><span class="c3-mb-sw" style="background:#d4d4cf"></span>Other districts, not allowed</li></ul>Our map of where the City of Myrtle Beach allows nightly rentals: the city's own map of the zones that allow them, drawn on its current zoning lines. The numbers are the parts of the city in the guide below. Map data: City of Myrtle Beach zoning; Horry County GIS; U.S. Census Bureau TIGER/Line.<ol class="c3-mb-key" aria-label="The numbers on the map"><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><a href="#grande-dunes">Grande Dunes</a></li><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><a href="#market-common">The Market Common</a></li><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><a href="#older-neighborhoods">The older neighborhoods of houses</a></li><li><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><a href="#oceanfront-condo">A condo on the oceanfront</a></li></ol></figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The allowed zones cover most of the oceanfront hotel and condo strip, the Broadway at the Beach area, stretches of the US 17 Bypass and US 501, and The Market Common's town center. That is about 5.1 of the city's 23.8 square miles.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 5.0 square miles are zoned for homes and ban nightly rentals. About 8 more are planned communities the city's map leaves out, such as Grande Dunes and the streets around The Market Common.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">How many homes fall on each side</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We counted every home in the city on the county's parcel map and placed each one on our map. About 3 in 4 condos are in a zone that allows nightly rentals. About 96 in 100 houses are not.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Which homes in the City of Myrtle Beach can rent by the night</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Kind of home</th><th scope="col">Homes in the city</th><th scope="col">In a zone that allows nightly rentals</th><th scope="col">For sale now in such a zone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Condos</th><td data-label="Homes in the city">About 16,900</td><td data-label="In a zone that allows nightly rentals">About 13,100, 3 in 4</td><td data-label="For sale now in such a zone">911 of 1,004</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Houses</th><td data-label="Homes in the city">About 10,300</td><td data-label="In a zone that allows nightly rentals">389, about 4 in 100</td><td data-label="For sale now in such a zone">43 of 264</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Villas and townhouses</th><td data-label="Homes in the city">About 850</td><td data-label="In a zone that allows nightly rentals">About 530</td><td data-label="For sale now in such a zone">33 of 86</td></tr></tbody></table></div><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/houses-and-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Older two-story houses on lawns along the beach at left, and two tall condo towers on the beach at right, with streets of houses under oak trees behind, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses and condo towers on the same beach in Myrtle Beach. The houses on the left are in a zone where nightly rentals are not allowed. The towers on the right are in one where they are.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The homes for sale today split the same way. Of the 668 condos for sale in oceanfront buildings inside the city, 667 are in an allowed zone. Of about 350 houses and townhouses for sale inside the city, 76 are.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Fewer than 30 houses in the city's residential zones are grandfathered for nightly rentals, because they were rented that way before the current zoning. No new ones can be added.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What a listing says is not the zoning</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">35 houses and townhouses for sale inside the city say in the listing that short-term rentals are allowed. 3 of those are not in a zone that allows them. We check the zoning on our map, and we read the HOA documents for any rule that would block your rental plan, before you offer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many communities ban renting the house out at all. We leave those out of your search when you plan to rent.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">The licence and the lodging tax</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Every rental in the city, short or long, needs a <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city business licence</a>, and its fee is figured on the rent you collect. On a stay under 90 days, the guest also pays about 13 percent in lodging taxes on top of the price. Our <a href="/invest/accommodations-tax/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">page on the lodging tax</a> shows who collects it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In 2024 the city also adopted a short-term rental conversion overlay for oceanfront buildings, Ordinance 2024-69. Our <a href="/invest/str-rules/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">short-term rental rules for every Grand Strand town</a> cover it, with the county's rules outside the city.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="city-or-county"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="City or county">Is a Myrtle Beach address in the City of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Usually not. About 3 in 4 houses and buildings with a Myrtle Beach mailing address are outside the city limits. Outside the city, the county's rules apply, not the city's rental map.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Myrtle Beach mailing addresses, by ZIP code</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">ZIP code</th><th scope="col">Houses and buildings with the address</th><th scope="col">Inside the city</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">29577</th><td data-label="Houses and buildings with the address">10,400</td><td data-label="Inside the city">About 85 in 100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">29572</th><td data-label="Houses and buildings with the address">5,300</td><td data-label="Inside the city">About 75 in 100</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">29579, which takes in Carolina Forest and Forestbrook</th><td data-label="Houses and buildings with the address">21,200</td><td data-label="Inside the city">280, about 1 in 75</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">29588, which takes in Socastee</th><td data-label="Houses and buildings with the address">19,000</td><td data-label="Inside the city">None</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In ZIP 29579, which takes in Carolina Forest and Forestbrook, only 280 of about 21,200 are inside the city. In 29588, which takes in Socastee, none are. Our <a href="/submarkets/carolina-forest/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">Carolina Forest guide</a> covers that area on its own.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">North Myrtle Beach is a separate city. A short-term rental there needs a business licence, and for now there is no special zoning or permit process beyond it. Our <a href="/submarkets/north-myrtle-beach/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">North Myrtle Beach guide</a> covers it.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="prices"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Prices">Are Myrtle Beach home prices dropping?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For condos, yes. Zillow's typical condo value in Myrtle Beach is about 2 percent lower than a year ago and about 14 percent below its high in 2024. For houses, no: the typical single-family value is up less than 1 percent in a year.</p><figure class="c3-gchart c3-mb-fig" style="max-width:640px"><span class="cap" style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1.1em;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .5rem">Zillow's typical home value in Myrtle Beach, houses and condos</span><ul class="c3-mb-legend"><li><span class="c3-mb-line" style="background:#2f6f8f"></span>Houses</li><li><span class="c3-mb-line" style="background:#c4783a"></span>Condos</li></ul>