233.7 22.6L236.5 22.7L239.3 23.2L242 23.6L244.8 23.7L247.5 23.8L250.3 24.1L253.1 24.8L255.8 25.9L258.6 27L261.3 27.9L264.1 28.3L266.9 28.5L269.6 28.7L272.4 28.8L275.2 28.8L277.9 28.5L280.7 28L283.4 27.6L286.2 27.5L289 27.4L291.7 27.3L294.5 27.1L297.2 27L300 26.7" fill="none" stroke="#2f6f8f" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M46 189.5L48.8 188.8L51.5 188.2L54.3 188L57 187.7L59.8 187.4L62.6 187.2L65.3 187.1L68.1 186.8L70.8 186.4L73.6 185.8L76.4 185.3L79.1 185L81.9 185L84.7 185L87.4 184.9L90.2 184.7L92.9 184.6L95.7 184.5L98.5 184.2L101.2 183.4L104 182.4L106.7 181.2L109.5 180.2L112.3 179.3L115 178.5L117.8 177.7L120.5 176.6L123.3 175.2L126.1 173.1L128.8 170.5L131.6 167.8L134.3 165.2L137.1 162.6L139.9 160L142.6 157.4L145.4 154.6L148.2 151.7L150.9 148.3L153.7 144L156.4 138.9L159.2 133.1L162 128.4L164.7 125.2L167.5 123.9L170.2 123.3L173 123.1L175.8 122.9L178.5 123.2L181.3 123.8L184 124.5L186.8 124.5L189.6 123.8L192.3 122.4L195.1 121.2L197.8 120.3L200.6 119.7L203.4 119.4L206.1 119.4L208.9 119.7L211.7 119.7L214.4 119.6L217.2 119.4L219.9 119.2L222.7 119.5L225.5 120.7L228.2 122.4L231 124L233.7 125.3L236.5 126.6L239.3 127.8L242 128.8L244.8 129.5L247.5 130L250.3 130.8L253.1 132L255.8 133.6L258.6 135.1L261.3 136.7L264.1 137.9L266.9 138.9L269.6 139.6L272.4 140L275.2 140.3L277.9 140.4L280.7 140.5L283.4 140.2L286.2 140.2L289 140.6L291.7 140.9L294.5 141.2L297.2 141.3L300 141.5" fill="none" stroke="#c4783a" stroke-width="3" stroke-linejoin="round"/><circle cx="219.9" cy="119.2" r="4" fill="#c4783a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.5"/><text class="cl" x="219.9" y="109.2" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a5226">Condo high</text><text class="cl" x="306" y="31.7" fill="#2f6f8f">$375k</text><text class="cl" x="306" y="146.5" fill="#8a5226">$207k</text></svg><figcaption>Monthly from January 2019. Houses here means Zillow's single-family homes.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The reason is supply. Months of supply means how long it would take to sell every home for sale now, at the past year's pace of sales.</p><div class="c3-mb-tiles"><div class="c3-mb-tile hot"><span class="big">About 18 months</span><span class="lbl">to sell every condo for sale in the city, at the past year's pace</span></div><div class="c3-mb-tile"><span class="big">About 4 months</span><span class="lbl">to sell every house and townhouse for sale in the city</span></div></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That makes the condo side a buyer's market, with room to negotiate. The house side has far fewer homes for sale than buyers in a year.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What homes resold for</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Condos that resold in the city in the past year went for about $175,000 in the middle, and half sold for between about $104,000 and $275,000. Houses, villas and townhouses went for about $305,000, and half sold for between about $170,000 and $530,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">New homes are rare inside the city. Builders sold 49 new homes here in the past year, about 2 percent of the 2,147 builder sales in the county.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Who owns them</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The two kinds of homes have different owners. About 3 in 4 houses are their owner's main home. Only about 1 in 8 condos are.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Homes in the city taxed as the owner's main home"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Homes in the city taxed as the owner's main home</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Kind of home</span><span role="columnheader">Share</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Houses</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.749" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 3 in 4</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Condos</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.118" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">About 1 in 8</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>South Carolina taxes a home its owner lives in at 4 percent of its value. Second homes and rentals are taxed at 6 percent.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 2 in 3 condos have their tax bill mailed outside South Carolina. About 1 in 8 houses do. What any one home is worth is a question for the nearby sales: our <a href="/sell/home-value/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">home value guide</a> shows them by area.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="oceanfront-buildings"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Oceanfront buildings">Which oceanfront condo buildings sell the most?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The cheapest ones. About 460 condos in oceanfront buildings inside the city resold in the past year, for about $148,000 in the middle. The buildings with the most sales were mostly small units at lower prices.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="Oceanfront condo buildings in the city with the most resales in the past year"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">Oceanfront condo buildings in the city with the most resales in the past year</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Building, middle price</span><span role="columnheader">Resales</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Tides, Driftwood and Oasis</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $53,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">60 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Landmark Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $102,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.85" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">51 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Coral Beach</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $85,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.6" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">36 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Caravelle Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $145,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.467" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">28 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Pinnacle Oceanfront Tower</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $150,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.383" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">23 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Long Bay Resort</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $170,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.35" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">21 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Monterey Bay Suites</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $150,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.317" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">19 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Dunes Village</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $269,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.283" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">17 sales</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">Sand Dunes Oceanfront</span><span class="dot" aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span><span class="f">middle price about $131,000</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.233" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">14 sales</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>Condos resold by their owners, from county deeds. Middle price: half sold for more, half for less. Landmark Resort is two condo associations at one site.</figcaption></figure><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-towers-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="782" alt="A row of oceanfront condo and hotel towers of 10 to 15 floors with pools in front, above a beach with umbrellas, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Oceanfront condo towers south of downtown Myrtle Beach, where the busiest buildings in the table stand. This stretch is in a zone where nightly rentals are allowed.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 3 in 4 of these buyers have their tax bill mailed outside South Carolina. Among buyers with an out-of-state tax bill, North Carolina, Pennsylvania, New York and Virginia are the most common, for the city as a whole.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many of these buildings run a rental program for their owners. At closing, buyers usually pay an HOA transfer fee and a few months of HOA dues in advance. Buildings with a rental program usually have so many investor owners that many common loans are not available for them. That also shows the building is run for renting.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The HOA fee and any special assessment differ by building. We get both for the building you like before you offer. Our pages on <a href="/hoa/special-assessments/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">special assessments</a> and <a href="/hoa/reserves/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">condo reserves</a> show what to look for, and <a href="/invest/condos/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">our condo investing guide</a> covers condos across the coast.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">Get the oceanfront condos for sale in Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="what-a-condo-earns"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="What a condo earns">Does an oceanfront condo in Myrtle Beach pay for itself?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">It can cover its own running costs and tax, with about $8,100 a year left over. Whether that is enough depends on the HOA fee, the insurance and any loan.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Here is the math for a typical one-bedroom. The middle asking price for a one-bedroom in an oceanfront building inside the city is about $160,000. The typical one-bedroom Airbnb in the Myrtle Beach market took in about $17,000 in a year, counting listings open only part of the year.</p><div class="c3-mb-sum" role="group" aria-label="A typical oceanfront one-bedroom, rented by the night, for a year"><span class="cap">A typical oceanfront one-bedroom, rented by the night, for a year</span><ol><li><span>What a typical one-bedroom takes in</span><strong>About $17,000</strong></li><li><span>Running costs: the Airbnb fee, cleaning, utilities, supplies, repairs, insurance and the permit</span><strong>About $6,500</strong></li><li><span>Property tax at the 6 percent rate, on $160,000</span><strong>About $2,400</strong></li><li class="tot"><span>Left each year for the HOA fee, the unit's insurance and any loan</span><strong>About $8,100</strong></li></ol></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">That is about $670 a month to pay the HOA fee, the unit's own insurance and any loan. The running costs use AirROI's share for its average listing run by its owner, about 38 percent, with no manager's fee in it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">We get the building's real HOA fee before you offer, so you see whether the $8,100 covers it. Our <a href="/invest/airbnb-income/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">nightly rental income by town</a> lets you compare all nine submarkets, and our <a href="/invest/long-term-rental/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">rental analyzer</a> runs the long-term rent instead.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Summer pays for the year</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The average listing takes in about $6,800 in July and about $1,340 in January, about 5 times as much. June, July and August bring in about 47 percent of a year's revenue.</p><style>main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact{padding-top:1rem;padding-bottom:.85rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .cap{margin-bottom:.7rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.1rem .9rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowheader]{line-height:1.3}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .b{height:.5rem;min-width:.5rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact .v{line-height:1.25}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact figcaption{margin-top:.8rem}@media (max-width:699px){main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=rowgroup]{gap:.45rem}main#main .c3-gchart.c3-gchart-compact [role=row]{gap:.05rem}}</style><figure class="c3-gchart c3-gchart-compact"><div role="table" aria-label="What the average Myrtle Beach nightly rental takes in, by month"><span class="cap" aria-hidden="true">What the average Myrtle Beach nightly rental takes in, by month</span><div role="rowgroup" class="sr"><div role="row"><span role="columnheader">Month</span><span role="columnheader">Revenue</span></div></div><div role="rowgroup"><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">January</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.197" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,340</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">February</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.247" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,680</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">March</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.372" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,530</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">April</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.412" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,800</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">May</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.481" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$3,270</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">June</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.893" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$6,070</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">July</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:1" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$6,800</span></span></div><div role="row"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">August</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.647" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$4,400</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">September</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.375" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,550</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">October</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.316" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$2,150</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">November</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.238" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,620</span></span></div><div role="row" class="ref"><span role="rowheader"><span class="n">December</span></span><span role="cell"><span class="b" style="--f:0.234" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="v">$1,590</span></span></div></div></div><figcaption>AirROI's figures for its Myrtle Beach market, each month averaged over the past two years. Its market reaches past the city limits.</figcaption></figure><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the off season like?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Quieter, not closed. In the off season, nothing closes except tourist attractions and water parks.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Hotels, restaurants, attractions and other leisure businesses in Horry County had about 31,300 private jobs in January 2025 and about 40,600 in July. That is about 9,300 more jobs in summer.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">At the 2020 Census, about 1 in 4 homes in the city were vacant on Census Day, meaning no one lived there as their usual home.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="where-to-live"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Where to live">Where should you live in Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the neighborhoods zoned for houses, where nightly rentals are not allowed and most homes are their owners' main homes. The numbers match the <a href="#rental-map" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">map above</a>.</p><h3 id="grande-dunes" data-toc="Grande Dunes" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span>Grande Dunes: the water on both sides</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Grande Dunes is a planned community on both sides of the Intracoastal Waterway, the inland water route behind the beach. It is the city's largest zoning district for houses, with about 2,150. The city's map does not allow nightly rentals in it.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 4 in 5 of its houses are their owners' main homes, more than in the older neighborhoods. Houses, villas and townhouses here resold for about $880,000 in the past year, the highest of the parts in this guide.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="grande-dunes" data-name="Grande Dunes"></div><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Grande%20Dunes">Get the homes for sale in Grande Dunes<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="market-common" data-toc="The Market Common" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span>The Market Common: a town built on an old air base</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The 3,936-acre former Myrtle Beach Air Force Base is now home to The Market Common and the neighborhoods around it, with thousands of new homes.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/market-common-valor-park-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/market-common-valor-park-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/best-neighborhoods/market-common-valor-park-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="900" alt="The Market Common from the air: streets of homes outlined in orange beside a lake, a dot labelled Valor Park at the edge of the shops, and ball fields and a lake labelled Grand Park" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title17/html/USCODE-2023-title17-chap1-sec105.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="U.S. government aerial photo. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">U.S. government aerial photo</a></span></div><figcaption>The Market Common from the air, with Grand Park and Valor Park.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 2,500 houses stand in the neighborhoods around it, among them Emmens Preserve, The Reserve, Sanctuary at Withers Preserve and Belle Harbor. About 6 in 7 are their owners' main homes, the highest share of the parts in this guide. Houses, villas and townhouses here resold for about $500,000.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The town center district is one the city's map allows for nightly rentals. Each neighborhood's HOA has its own rules, and we read them before you count on renting.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="market-common" data-name="The Market Common"></div><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=The%20Market%20Common">Get the homes for sale in The Market Common<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="older-neighborhoods" data-toc="The older neighborhoods of houses" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span>The older neighborhoods of houses: older streets zoned for houses only</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">These are the neighborhoods the R zones protect: around The Dunes Club and Pine Lakes, Myrtle Heights and Oak Park, Forest Dunes and Northwood. Some streets reach the ocean, with houses on lawns behind the dunes.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/submarkets-myrtle-beach/oceanfront-houses-from-the-ocean-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="782" alt="Two-story houses on wide green lawns behind the dunes, with wooden walkways to the beach and oak trees behind, seen from a plane over the ocean in Myrtle Beach" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: U.S. Geological Survey. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: U.S. Geological Survey</a></span></div><figcaption>Houses on wide lawns facing the beach, on the older streets north of downtown Myrtle Beach. Nightly rentals are not allowed here.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">They hold about 3,150 houses, and about 7 in 10 are their owners' main homes. Houses here resold for about $550,000 in the past year. The range was wide: half sold for between about $336,000 and $854,000.</p><style>.c3ph-f{position:relative;margin:0;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--ivory-2)}.c3ph-f img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.c3ph-cr{position:absolute;right:0;bottom:0;max-width:100%;padding:1.6rem .6rem .35rem 2.6rem;font:400 .625rem/1.3 var(--sans);letter-spacing:.01em;color:#fff;text-align:right;background:radial-gradient(farthest-side at 100% 100%,rgba(28,32,40,.72),rgba(28,32,40,.4) 55%,rgba(28,32,40,0));white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;pointer-events:none}.c3ph-cr a{color:#fff;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5);text-underline-offset:2px;pointer-events:auto;padding:10px 0 6px}.c3ph-hero{margin:1.6rem 0 2rem}.c3ph-hero .c3ph-f{border-radius:8px}.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:4/3}@media (min-width:700px){.c3ph-hero img{aspect-ratio:16/9}}.c3ph-hero figcaption{color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;line-height:1.5;margin-top:.55rem}</style><figure class="c3ph-hero" style="margin:1.6rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:680px;"><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/buyers/no-hoa/pine-lakes-clubhouse-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/buyers/no-hoa/pine-lakes-clubhouse-600w.webp 600w, /images/buyers/no-hoa/pine-lakes-clubhouse-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 680px" width="1200" height="675" alt="The large white Pine Lakes clubhouse with a row of tall columns, black shutters and dormer windows in a gray roof" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Pubdog. License: Public domain" title="License: Public domain">Photo: Pubdog</a></span></div><figcaption>The clubhouse of the Pine Lakes golf course, among the older neighborhoods of houses.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The rule shows in the condos too. In the R zones, about 1 in 3 condos is its owner's main home, against about 1 in 18 in the zones that allow nightly rentals.</p><div class="hx-strip" data-place="pine-lakes" data-name="Pine Lakes"></div><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach's%20older%20neighborhoods">Get the homes for sale in Myrtle Beach's older neighborhoods<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p><h3 id="oceanfront-condo" data-toc="A condo on the oceanfront" class="c3-mb-h3" style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.3rem;color:var(--navy);margin:2rem 0 .6rem;line-height:1.3"><span class="c3-mb-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span>A condo on the oceanfront: the beach at the door</span></h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You can live in an oceanfront condo too. Expect most of your neighbors to be guests: in the zones that allow nightly rentals, only about 1 in 18 condos is someone's main home.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For a building where more people live all year, look at the condos in the R zones. Condos there resold for about $270,000 in the past year, against about $155,000 in the zones that allow nightly rentals. There were only a few dozen such sales, and the rental-zone units are often hotel-room size.</p><p class="c3-offer"><a class="c3-offer-pill" href="/contact/?place=Myrtle%20Beach">Get the condos for sale in Myrtle Beach<span class="c3-offer-ar" aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></span></a></p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="yearly-cost"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Yearly cost">What does it cost to own a home in Myrtle Beach each year?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, a home you live in pays about $404 a year in property tax for every $100,000 of the county's value. A second home or rental pays about $1,528.</p><style>.c3-cc{margin:1.4rem 0 1.8rem;max-width:960px}.c3-cc table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.45;color:var(--muted)}.c3-cc caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;line-height:1.4;padding:0 0 .7rem}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{padding:.6rem .7rem;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);overflow-wrap:break-word}.c3-cc thead th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;font-size:1em;border-bottom:2px solid var(--navy);vertical-align:bottom}.c3-cc tbody th{color:var(--navy);font-weight:600}.c3-cc .n{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.c3-cc .i{display:inline-flex;vertical-align:-4px;margin-right:.45rem;color:var(--brass-ink)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:#fff}@media (max-width:39.999em){.c3-cc table,.c3-cc tbody,.c3-cc tr,.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{display:block;width:auto}.c3-cc caption{display:block}.c3-cc thead{position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap}.c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass);margin:0 0 .8rem;padding:.5rem 0 .6rem}section[style*="background:var(--ivory-2)"] .c3-cc tbody tr{background:var(--ivory)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self{background:#fff!important;border:2px solid var(--brass)}.c3-cc tr.c3-self>*{background:transparent}.c3-cc th,.c3-cc td{border:0;padding:.2rem 1rem}.c3-cc tbody th{display:flex;align-items:center;font-size:1.1em;padding-bottom:.35rem}.c3-cc tbody th .i{flex:none;vertical-align:0}.c3-cc tbody th a{display:inline-block;padding:.5rem 0}.c3-cc .n{text-align:left}.c3-cc td[data-label]::before{content:attr(data-label) ": ";color:var(--navy);font-weight:500}}</style><div class="c3-cc"><table><caption>Property tax each year inside the City of Myrtle Beach</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">The home</th><th scope="col">A home you live in</th><th scope="col">A second home or rental</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Every $100,000 of value</th><td data-label="A home you live in">$404</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">$1,530</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A $305,000 house</th><td data-label="A home you live in">About $1,230</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $4,660</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">A $175,000 condo</th><td data-label="A home you live in">About $710</td><td data-label="A second home or rental">About $2,670</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">You must apply for the lower rate on the home you live in. Our <a href="/buyers/property-taxes/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">property tax guide</a> shows how, with the rate for every town.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Flood zones</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About 1 in 4 condos in the city is in FEMA's high-risk flood zone, and 1,105 of them are in the zone at the ocean's edge where waves add to the risk. Only about 1 in 23 houses is in the high-risk zone.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">A condo building insures the building and passes the cost to owners through the HOA fee. Of the city's zoning districts with 50 or more houses, the Meridian and Summit at Meridian district on the west side has the highest share in the high-risk zone: 40 percent of its 513 houses.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Our <a href="/buyers/coastal-insurance/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">coastal insurance guide</a> explains the policies a home here needs, and our <a href="/buyers/undisclosed-flooding/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline">flood history guide</a> shows how we find out whether a house has flooded.</p></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="pros-and-cons"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Pros and cons">What are the pros and cons of Myrtle Beach?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">The good points are the beach, the choice of homes and the growth. The hard ones are the condo market, the season and the flood zone at the ocean.</p><style>.c3-pc{display:grid;gap:1rem;max-width:960px;margin:1.2rem 0 1.6rem}@media (min-width:760px){.c3-pc{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;align-items:start}}.c3-pc>div{padding:1.1rem 1.2rem .6rem}.c3-pc h3{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:1.15rem;font-weight:600;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem}.c3-pc,.c3-pc ul{font-size:1em}.c3-pc ul{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.c3-pc li{display:flex;gap:.7rem;align-items:flex-start;color:var(--muted);font-size:var(--read,1.0625rem);line-height:1.7;margin:0 0 .9rem}.c3-pc li svg{flex:none;margin-top:.3rem}.c3-pc .c3-pc-do{display:block;color:var(--navy);font-weight:500;margin-top:.2rem}</style><div class="c3-pc"><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--brass)"><h3>Pros</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The rental zoning keeps the house neighborhoods lived in: about 3 in 4 houses are their owners' main homes.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>Condos resell for about $175,000, a way to own at the beach for less than a house.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>The airport is inside the city.</span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="11" fill="var(--brass)"/><path d="M6.2 11.4l3.1 3.1 6.5-6.7" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg><span>About 40,900 people lived in the city in 2025, up about 15 percent since 2020.</span></li></ul></div><div style="background:var(--ivory-2);border-top:3px solid var(--muted)"><h3>Cons</h3><ul><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Condo prices are falling, and there are about 18 months of condos for sale. <span class="c3-pc-do">We help you pick the building and negotiate the price.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Rental income comes mostly in summer. <span class="c3-pc-do">We plan the year with you before you buy.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>About 1 in 4 condos is in a high-risk flood zone. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the flood zone and the building's insurance before you offer.</span></span></li><li><svg aria-hidden="true" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 22 22"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.6"/><path d="M6.8 11h8.4" stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg><span>Most houses cannot be rented by the night. <span class="c3-pc-do">We check the zoning of any address on our map.</span></span></li></ul></div></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory-2)" id="myrtle-beach-real-estate-faq"><div class="wrap"><p style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brass);margin-bottom:.5rem;font-weight:600">Common questions</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3">Myrtle Beach real estate FAQ</h2><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Can you do short-term rentals in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Inside the city, only in the zones that allow them: about 3 in 4 condos and about 4 in 100 houses. Every R zone except RMV bans rentals under 90 days.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's market?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">For condos, yes: there are about 18 months of condos for sale, and prices are falling. For houses, no: there are about 4 months of supply.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">Is Carolina Forest in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">No. Carolina Forest has a Myrtle Beach address, but only about 1 in 75 homes in its ZIP code, 29579, is inside the city.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the property tax on a second home in Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">About $1,528 a year for every $100,000 of the county's value inside the city, against about $404 for a home you live in.</p><h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.25rem;color:var(--navy);margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem">What is the difference between Myrtle Beach and North Myrtle Beach?</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">They are two separate cities. A short-term rental in North Myrtle Beach needs a business licence, and for now there is no special zoning or permit process beyond it.</p><p style="font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.7;max-width:760px;margin-top:1.6rem"><strong style="color:var(--navy)">Sources:</strong> <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R1468.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city STR notice</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/departments/planning_and_zoning_department.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city zoning</a>, <a href="https://www.cityofmyrtlebeach.com/careers/business/business_faq.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city licence FAQ</a>, <a href="https://cityofmyrtlebeach.com/news_detail_T6_R729.php" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">city air base history</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycounty.org/parcelapp/rest/services/HorryCountyGISApp/MapServer" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Horry County GIS</a>, <a href="https://acclaimweb.horrycounty.org/AcclaimWeb/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">county deeds</a>, <a href="https://www.zillow.com/research/data/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zillow Research</a>, <a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AirROI</a>, <a href="https://www2.census.gov/programs-surveys/popest/datasets/2020-2025/cities/totals/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Census estimates</a>, <a href="https://www.bls.gov/cew/" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">BLS QCEW</a>, <a href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">FEMA flood maps</a>, <a href="https://www.horrycountysc.gov/media/kufln4qp/tax-levy-2026_2.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2026 tax levy</a>, <a href="https://dor.sc.gov/sites/dor/files/forms/ST575.pdf" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SCDOR ST-575</a>, <a href="https://www.nmb.us/833/Short-term-Rentals" style="color:var(--navy);text-decoration:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NMB rentals</a>. Our counts from city zoning, its 2021 rental-zone map, county parcels, FEMA zones and the past year's deeds. Listings in aggregate from CCMLS. Not legal or tax advice.</p><style>.c3ph-credits{margin:2rem 0 1rem;padding:1rem 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.55;max-width:760px}.c3ph-credits .c3ph-h{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.8rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--navy);margin:0 0 .4rem}.c3ph-credits [role=listitem]{margin:0 0 .3rem}.c3ph-credits a{color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:rgba(28,32,40,.3);text-underline-offset:2px}</style><div class="c3ph-credits"><div class="c3ph-h" id="photo-credits">Photo credits</div><div role="list" aria-labelledby="photo-credits"><div role="listitem">Houses and condo towers on the same beach in Myrtle Beach. The houses on the left are in a zone where nightly rentals are not allowed. The towers on the right are in one where they are. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo and cut 1x1, 4x3 and 16x9 crops.</div><div role="listitem">Oceanfront condo towers south of downtown Myrtle Beach, where the busiest buildings in the table stand. This stretch is in a zone where nightly rentals are allowed. Photo: U.S. Geological Survey, <a href="https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public domain</a>, via <a href="https://doi.org/10.5066/F7N877XX" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">U.S. Geological Survey</a>. Chapter3 Realty resized the photo.</div><div role="listitem">The Market Common from the air, with Grand Park and Valor Park. Photo: NOAA National Geodetic Survey, <a href="https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USC