ar. That compares with 39% for the South Carolina average. July is usually the busiest month. How much does an Airbnb cost per night in Myrtle Beach? The average booked night in Myrtle Beach cost $257 before fees. Half of listings charge between $160 and $285, so bedroom count and location move the price more than the average suggests. Do you need a permit for an Airbnb in Myrtle Beach? Yes, in the zones that allow stays under 90 days, with a City of Myrtle Beach business license; most residential neighborhoods are closed to short-term rentals. The Myrtle Beach Airbnb regulations set out the permit, its cost, the taxes on a stay and the operating limits, each linked to its official source. Is Airbnb profitable in Myrtle Beach? Yes, when it's run well. The average Myrtle Beach Airbnb grossed $25,807 in the 12 months to September 2026, 31% below the South Carolina average of $37,525. Run by its owner, with the cleaning fee covering the cleaner and everyday costs for Airbnb's fee, utilities, supplies, upkeep and insurance, $15,977 a year (about $1,330 a month) is left before the mortgage or rent. A home that costs less than that to own or rent makes a profit, and a listing at the top-quarter mark leaves about $2,310 a month. Check a specific home in the Airbnb estimator . When is Airbnb peak season in Myrtle Beach? July usually pays best, averaging $6,800 per active listing over the past two years, and January usually pays least. The month-by-month table above shows how the latest 12 months played out. What is the Airbnb RevPAR in Myrtle Beach? Each night a Myrtle Beach listing was open to book earned $106 on average over the past year, booked or not. That figure, revenue per available night (RevPAR), folds price and occupancy into one number; the top 10% of listings made $204 or more. How far in advance do guests book Airbnbs in Myrtle Beach? Myrtle Beach stays were booked 52 days (about seven weeks) before arrival on average over the past year, so most of a month is booked well before it starts. How long do guests stay at Airbnbs in Myrtle Beach? The average Myrtle Beach Airbnb stay lasted 4.7 nights over the past year. A listing took 19 reservations over the year on average. How are Airbnbs in Myrtle Beach rated? Guests rate Myrtle Beach Airbnbs 4.66 out of 5 on average. Guests score location highest and cleanliness lowest. What are the best neighborhoods for Airbnb in Myrtle Beach? Broadway at the Beach, Myrtle Beach Boardwalk and Promenade and West Myrtle Beach draw the most short-term rental interest in Myrtle Beach. The neighborhood guide explains what brings guests to each. How many Airbnbs are there in Myrtle Beach? AirROI counted 8,698 active Airbnb listings in Myrtle Beach as of September 2026. The closest tracked market is Fantasy Harbour , 5 km away. How much are Airbnb cleaning fees in Myrtle Beach? In Myrtle Beach, about nine in ten listings add a cleaning fee, and the typical fee is about $151. Method About This Data Figures on this page cover 8,698 active Airbnb listings in Myrtle Beach from October 2025 to September 2026 (trailing twelve months). AirROI refreshes them monthly from listing-level booking and calendar data covering 20+ million properties worldwide. Money figures are in U.S. dollars. Annual revenue averages every listing active during the period, including those listed for only part of it; monthly figures average the listings active in each month; the tier lists show the spread. Neighborhood descriptions are AI-assisted. See the methodology for definitions. Cite this data AirROI. (2026). Myrtle Beach, SC Airbnb market data, October 2025–September 2026 [Data set]. https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data/united-states/south-carolina/myrtle-beach Copy citation Embed these numbers HTML embed code for Myrtle Beach, SC Airbnb data <div style="font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;border:1px solid #e5e7eb;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px;max-width:440px;line-height:1.5"><a href="https://www.airroi.com/airbnb-data